<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 50 0 R
/T (Students oftenknow what they are avoiding but rarely understand why. Procrastination Spy: Operation Deadline is a C++ console application built on Object Oriented Programming principles that turns the psychology of avoidance into an interactive "spy mission". Instead of tracking what students do, it analyzes what they avoid, and interrogates their excuses.)
/E (Students oftenknow what they are avoiding but rarely understand why. Procrastination Spy: Operation Deadline is a C++ console application built on Object Oriented Programming principles that turns the psychology of avoidance into an interactive "spy mission". Instead of tracking what students do, it analyzes what they avoid, and interrogates their excuses.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 50 0 R
/T (The application has three unique mechanics: an Interrogation Room that detects contradictions between a stated excuse and the real reason, a Mole Hunt that identifies the student's number one distraction and assigns a weekly mission, and a Threat Level Countdown that maps deadline urgency. The project demonstrates inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation, composition and file handling while remaining lightweight and useful for student self-reflection.)
/E (The application has three unique mechanics: an Interrogation Room that detects contradictions between a stated excuse and the real reason, a Mole Hunt that identifies the student's number one distraction and assigns a weekly mission, and a Threat Level Countdown that maps deadline urgency. The project demonstrates inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation, composition and file handling while remaining lightweight and useful for student self-reflection.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
