/S /H3
/P 50 0 R
/T (Every student procrastinates. Most productivity tools focus on doing more: timers, habit trackers and to-do lists. None of them ask the uncomfortable question: "Why did you avoid this in the first place?" Procrastination is usually not laziness. It is more often fear, overwhelm or self-deception. A tool that surfaces these patterns is genuinely valuable.)
/E (Every student procrastinates. Most productivity tools focus on doing more: timers, habit trackers and to-do lists. None of them ask the uncomfortable question: "Why did you avoid this in the first place?" Procrastination is usually not laziness. It is more often fear, overwhelm or self-deception. A tool that surfaces these patterns is genuinely valuable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [28]
